ones, with postings on any topic, off-charter or on-charter,
and so forge approval headers to overwhelm moderated
newsgroups with their ravings, and also trash unmoderated
groups. There is a set of newsgroups they attack regularly
in an ongoing war, and a "usual" set of attackers.

These people are not in good mental health (but then,
neither am I). The argument that freedom of speech doesn't
mean I have to print your letter in my newspaper has no
effect on them. In their minds freedom of speech is an
absolute, and no one should be permitted to control a venue
where they can read but not write.

The Net has always _had_ an all-purpose newsgroup that meets
the need for a group in which any post on any topic is
welcome, and so satisfies the requirement that Usenet
support "free speech".

It is named misc.misc.

So, though my success rate is too low in my advanced state
of senility, I try to crosspost all my articles there just
to demonstrate that no-one wants to participate in such a
group.  It has been write-only for years, since the alt
heirarchy made creating a newsgroup for any desired topic
painless, and mostly is just a universal spam catcher except
for my postings there.

